Let the build say where the assets and the database are

Craft opens its shaders and textures by relative path - `load_file("shaders/...")`
and `load_png_texture("textures/...")` - and its database as `craft.db`. That is
right for a program started from its own directory, and there is no such thing
here: a payload is called rather than spawned, the package is mounted read-only
at `/app0`, and the one writable place is elsewhere again.

**Both are made overridable rather than changed.** `CRAFT_DATA_DIR` is empty
unless the build sets it, and `craft_data_path` then returns the path it was
given, byte for byte - so every platform that has a working directory behaves
exactly as before. `DB_PATH` gains an `#ifndef` for the same reason. This port
passes `-DCRAFT_DATA_DIR=\"/app0\"` and a `DB_PATH` under `/data`.

The prefix is applied in `util.c`'s two loaders rather than at the eight call
sites in `main.c`, because that is where the filesystem is actually touched: a
future asset loaded through either function is covered without another patch,
and the two `fprintf` diagnostics now report the path that was really opened
rather than the one that was asked for.

An absolute path is passed through unprefixed, so a caller that already knows
where it is keeps working.

diff --git a/src/config.h b/src/config.h
index 599bbc1..30524b8 100644
--- a/src/config.h
+++ b/src/config.h
@@ -9,7 +9,15 @@
 #define VSYNC 1
 #define SCROLL_THRESHOLD 0.1
 #define MAX_MESSAGES 4
+#ifndef DB_PATH
 #define DB_PATH "craft.db"
+#endif
+
+/* Where the shaders and textures live, prefixed to a relative asset path by util.c. Empty by
+   default, which is exactly the behaviour every platform with a working directory had before. */
+#ifndef CRAFT_DATA_DIR
+#define CRAFT_DATA_DIR ""
+#endif
 #define USE_CACHE 1
 #define DAY_LENGTH 600
 #define INVERT_MOUSE 0
diff --git a/src/util.c b/src/util.c
index 9e1d0b1..439ff2b 100644
--- a/src/util.c
+++ b/src/util.c
@@ -1,11 +1,24 @@
 #include <math.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
 #include <errno.h>
+#include "config.h"
 #include "lodepng.h"
 #include "matrix.h"
 #include "util.h"
 
+/* Resolve an asset path against CRAFT_DATA_DIR, which is empty unless the build sets it - so on
+   every platform that has a working directory this is what it always was. */
+static void craft_data_path(const char *path, char *out, size_t n) {
+    if (CRAFT_DATA_DIR[0] == '\0' || path[0] == '/') {
+        snprintf(out, n, "%s", path);
+    }
+    else {
+        snprintf(out, n, "%s/%s", CRAFT_DATA_DIR, path);
+    }
+}
+
